WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:08.286
The next day I awoke after sleeping for twelve hours. As usual Conseil came to my room to see if I needed anything.

2
00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:13.436
"Did you sleep well?" he asked as he did every day when we were living on land.

3
00:00:13.437 --> 00:00:16.777
"Quite well," I replied. "Where's Ned?"

4
00:00:16.778 --> 00:00:23.372
"Still sleeping, Master. Ned appears to have plenty of practice at sleeping. He sleeps so soundly that I . . ."

5
00:00:23.373 --> 00:00:28.539
Conseil chattered on, but I didn't respond because I was thinking about Captain Nemo.

6
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.197
Why hadn't we seen him last night? I was sure he'd make an appearance today.

7
00:00:33.198 --> 00:00:41.197
As soon as I was dressed, I went into the gallery. It was deserted. I plunged into studying the shells in the glass cases.

8
00:00:41.198 --> 00:00:45.428
I also enjoyed the huge albums filled with rare marine plants.

9
00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:50.095
Even though the plants were dried, they retained their lovely colors.

10
00:00:50.096 --> 00:00:53.928
The whole day passed without Captain Nemo honoring me with a visit.

11
00:00:53.929 --> 00:01:00.253
The panels in the museum room did not open. Perhaps he did not wish us to tire of the beautiful view.

12
00:01:00.254 --> 00:01:07.079
The Nautilus continued on its course, traveling at a depth ranging from 150 to 180 feet.

13
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.150
The next day, November 10, I didn't see a single member of the ship's crew. Ned

14
00:01:12.151 --> 00:01:19.238
and Conseil spent most of the day with me, and they were astonished at the inexplicable absence of the captain. Was

15
00:01:19.239 --> 00:01:25.317
this eccentric man ill? Had he changed his mind about how he was going to treat us? But

16
00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:34.468
as Conseil pointed out, we were still free to roam the submarine and we were always provided with delicious and abundant food. Our

17
00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:42.627
host kept his part of the bargain, and we couldn't complain because this voyage really was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity. Early

18
00:01:42.628 --> 00:01:50.460
the next morning, November 11, I could smell fresh sea air, so I knew that the Nautilus had risen to the surface. I

19
00:01:50.461 --> 00:01:55.056
went up on the platform, where I fully expected to meet Captain Nemo. It

20
00:01:55.057 --> 00:02:00.548
was six o'clock; the sky was cloudy and the sea was gray but calm. I

21
00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:04.111
saw no one except the pilot in his glass cage. I

22
00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:10.190
inhaled the salt air with delight as the sun's rays gradually burned away the fog. I

23
00:02:10.191 --> 00:02:18.444
was admiring the sunrise when I heard someone climbing up to the platform. I turned, fully expecting to greet Captain Nemo. But

24
00:02:18.445 --> 00:02:25.095
it was only his second-in-command, his lieutenant, the other man that I'd met on our first day onboard the Nautilus .

25
00:02:25.096 --> 00:02:28.278
He climbed onto the platform without seeming to see me.

26
00:02:28.279 --> 00:02:33.341
Putting his telescope to his eye, he scanned the horizon with great attention.

27
00:02:33.342 --> 00:02:40.421
When he'd finished, he went to the hatch and called down, " Nautron respoc lorni

28
00:02:40.422 --> 00:02:49.326
virch ." What these words meant I couldn't say, but I have remembered this sentence because he repeated it every day under the exact

29
00:02:49.327 --> 00:02:53.826
same conditions. Having uttered these words, Nemo's lieutenant descended through

30
00:02:53.827 --> 00:02:59.579
the hatch. I thought that the Nautilus was about to resume its underwater voyage, so I went down to

31
00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:06.910
my cabin. Five days passed like this without any change in our situation. Every morning I mounted

32
00:03:06.911 --> 00:03:13.636
the platform. The same man said the same sentence in the same strange language. Captain Nemo did

33
00:03:13.637 --> 00:03:16.882
not appear. I had made up my mind that I would never see

34
00:03:16.883 --> 00:03:23.725
him again. But on November 16, I returned to my cabin with Ned and Conseil and found an envelope on

35
00:03:23.726 --> 00:03:29.376
my table. I opened it impatiently and read a note in bold,

36
00:03:29.377 --> 00:03:31.705
clear handwriting. The note was worded

37
00:03:31.706 --> 00:03:34.955
as follows: To Professor Aronnax onboard

38
00:03:34.956 --> 00:03:43.709
the Nautilus: Captain Nemo invites Professor Aronnax to a hunting party that will take place tomorrow morning in his forests on the island of

39
00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:47.622
Crespo. The captain hopes that nothing will prevent the professor from being

40
00:03:47.623 --> 00:03:51.443
present. The professor's companions are also invited to join the

41
00:03:51.444 --> 00:03:54.694
hunt. Captain Nemo, commander of the

42
00:03:54.695 --> 00:03:57.177
Nautilus "A hunt!" exclaimed

43
00:03:57.178 --> 00:04:02.193
Ned. "And in his forests on the island of Crespo!" added

44
00:04:02.194 --> 00:04:05.932
Conseil. "So it sounds like the captain is going ashore," said

45
00:04:05.933 --> 00:04:08.264
Ned. I read the note

46
00:04:08.265 --> 00:04:11.526
again. "It certainly does seem that way," I

47
00:04:11.527 --> 00:04:15.685
said. "Well, we must definitely accept this invitation," said

48
00:04:15.686 --> 00:04:20.169
Ned. "All this fish is fine, but I wouldn't mind eating some fresh

49
00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.764
venison." I was still trying to make sense of Captain Nemo's

50
00:04:23.765 --> 00:04:29.256
invitation. He planned to go hunting in a forest yet had a strong aversion to anything on

51
00:04:29.257 --> 00:04:34.169
land. "I've never heard of this island," I said. "Let's find out where it

52
00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:40.820
is." I consulted the map and showed my companions a tiny island lost in the middle of the northern

53
00:04:40.821 --> 00:04:45.153
Pacific. I also noted that we were about 800 leagues from our starting

54
00:04:45.154 --> 00:04:51.653
point. "If Captain Nemo sometimes does go on dry land," I said, "he certainly chooses remote

55
00:04:51.654 --> 00:04:56.320
islands." The rest of the day passed without another word or visit from the

56
00:04:56.321 --> 00:05:01.717
captain. When I awoke the next morning, I could feel that the Nautilus was perfectly

57
00:05:01.718 --> 00:05:06.638
still. I dressed quickly and entered the gallery, where I found Captain

58
00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:14.376
Nemo. He made no reference to his absence for the past eight days, but simply asked if we would be accompanying him

59
00:05:14.377 --> 00:05:24.463
today. "We will," I replied. "But I'm puzzled by one thing: How can you own forests on Crespo Island if you've cut all ties with

60
00:05:24.464 --> 00:05:34.042
land?" "My forests don't bask in the heat and light of the sun," he replied. "They aren't on land; they're actual underwater

61
00:05:34.043 --> 00:05:39.376
forests." "You're offering to take me to real underwater forests?" I couldn't believe

62
00:05:39.377 --> 00:05:45.011
it. "Yes, Professor, and without getting your feet wet. Now come eat breakfast with

63
00:05:45.012 --> 00:05:50.670
me. There aren't any restaurants on Crespo, and it will be a long time before you have

64
00:05:50.671 --> 00:05:54.274
supper." While we ate, I asked the captain some

65
00:05:54.275 --> 00:06:01.495
questions. "I'm familiar with a diving apparatus that lets a man breathe underwater, but he must stay tethered to a ship," I

66
00:06:01.496 --> 00:06:08.621
began. "Then there's a diving suit that allows a man to leave the ship, but it only contains a limited amount of air in a backpack.

67
00:06:08.622 --> 00:06:11.011
Which one will we be using?"

68
00:06:11.012 --> 00:06:18.995
"A version of the diving suit," said Captain Nemo. "I've improved it so that a man can stay underwater for nine or ten hours."

69
00:06:18.996 --> 00:06:25.320
"But how will we be able to see in the dark waters? And a regular gun won't fire in the water."

70
00:06:25.321 --> 00:06:35.306
The captain smiled. "Don't worry. I've invented both a light and a gun that will work underwater. Are you ready to go hunting?"

71
00:06:35.307 --> 00:06:40.726
We left the dining room and as we passed my companions' cabin, I called for them to join us.

72
00:06:40.727 --> 00:06:45.988
Near the engine room we came to a small room where we found a dozen diving suits.

73
00:06:45.989 --> 00:06:50.964
"Oh no," said Ned. "I'm not getting into one of those."

74
00:06:50.965 --> 00:06:56.861
"But there's no alternative," I said. "The forests of Crespo are underwater."

75
00:06:56.862 --> 00:07:02.789
"Underwater?" Ned seemed to realize that his dream of eating venison was slipping away.

76
00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:08.520
"Unless someone forces me, I won't be going with you," the harpooner replied firmly.

77
00:07:08.521 --> 00:07:12.599
"No one will force you, Mr. Land," said Captain Nemo.

78
00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.615
"Are you coming with us?" I asked Conseil.

79
00:07:15.616 --> 00:07:21.865
"I follow my master wherever he goes," replied my loyal servant.

